 of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1600 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Support Initial Variant Condition Keys\nDescription: When the VARCOND key field in an access was flagged as Initial Value Allowed and a condition record with an empty variant condition key was maintained, the Pricing service used to return different results from the pricing in the back end. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-10\nValid as Of: 2025-01-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 51 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: Environment Indicators in User Documentation\nDescription: In support of the release of SAP Cloud Integration for data services on SAP BTP Kyma runtime and with the service's being in use simultaneously on the Neo environment, indicators have been added in various places within the user documentation to reflect when information pertains to one environment or the other.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-24\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 52 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Documentation update only: User Activation Emails\nDescription: Finish Setting Up a Standard User has been updated to reflect that, when using SAP Identity Authentication (IAS) on the Neo environment or Kyma runtime, SAP Cloud Integration for data services does not send emails to notify users when they have been activated.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-19\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 53 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma,Neo\nTitle: IBP JDBC Supported on the Neo Environment Only\nDescription: IBP JDBC and other cloud applications such as SAP Lumira Cloud and SAP HANA are not supported on SAP Cloud Integration for data services on Kyma runtime. Information in the user documentation that refers to these has been marked as 'Neo environment only'.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-08\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 54 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Notifications and Renewal of Expiring IdP Certificates\nDescription: As the expiration date of an IdP certificate approaches, administrators and security administrators will receive email notifications. You can use the new Renew Certificate button to initiate the renewal. If not renewed before its expiration, the certificate will automatically be renewed by the system. Renewed certificates must be manually configured on the IdP. Also, IdP certificate renewals will appear in the Security log. For more information, see Notifications and Renewal of Expiring IdP Certificates and Security Log.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-08\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 55 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration for Data Services\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Release Number Added to Administration Tab\nDescription: The SAP Cloud Integration for data services release number you are using now appears on the Administration tab beside your current server version. For more information, see Administration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Database and Data Management\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: 2509\n\n--- Record 56 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Pipelines\nDescription: You can now upload a maximum number of 3000 documents per pipeline with the document grounding capability.  See Set Up Content Ingestion.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-25\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 57 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Support for Images and Tables Embedded in PDF Documents\nDescription: The document grounding capability supports now images and tables embedded in PDF documents.  See Set Up Document Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-25\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 58 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Use SAP Build Work Zone to Access SAP Task Center When Both Are in Different Subaccounts\nDescription: You can now use SAP Build Work Zone as your central point of entry for accessing your SAP Task Center, when both are in different subaccounts. For more information, see Connect SAP Task Center and SAP Build Work Zone in Different Subaccounts.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-25\nValid as Of: 2025-09-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 59 ---\nComponent: Intelligent Situation Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Intelligent Situation Automation\nDescription: Intelligent Situation Automation is being deprecated. The service will be under maintenance only mode till the end-of-service date, 6 months from the announcement or when the last contract commitment is fulfilled. For more information, see this blog post.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-24\nValid as Of: 2025-09-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 60 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway", " mode till the end-of-service date, 6 months from the announcement or when the last contract commitment is fulfilled. For more information, see this blog post.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-24\nValid as Of: 2025-09-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 60 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.2.3\nDescription: We've fixed the jwt and ext-auth setup of RequestAuthentication, which is now created for all workloads, regardless of whether they have the app label or not. For more information, see issue #2237.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-22\nValid as Of: 2025-09-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2381 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Condition and skip update - changed behavior\nDescription: As of September 24, 2024, Identity Provisioning will change the behavior of target transformations that contain a combination of condition and skip operations for updates. For example: Code Syntax  \"condition\": \"$.groups empty false\",\n\"skipOperations\": [\"update\"],   Currently, the skip operation is evaluated before the condition. If any users or groups have been updated in the source system, they are marked as skipped in the logs, and Identity Provisioning does not proceed to evaluate the condition. As a result, users or groups that do not meet the condition are not deleted as they should be.  Following the change, the condition will be evaluated first. Users and groups who do not match the condition will be skipped. After the condition is evaluated, the skip operation will determine whether the remaining users will be skipped or provisioned.  See Transformation Expressions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2382 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: isValidEmail function supports new value\nDescription: The conditional function isValidEmail can now accept the following value $.emails[*].value. In cases where users have multiple emails, this function will validate each email in the emails array.  See Transformation Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2383 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: OpenID Connect\nDescription: You can use certificate to authenticate the system as administrator when you call Identity Authentication Token Endpoint for Client Credentials Flow. SeeConfigure the Client to Call Identity Authentication Token Endpoint for Client Credentials Flow .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2384 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Read and proxy read transformation changes\nDescription: The mapping which omits the display of groups under the user entity is removed from the default read and proxy read transformations of the Identity Authentication and Local Identity Directory connectors. This makes possible filtering users by groups display name when using condition in the target system.  See Identity Authentication and Local Identity Directory.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2385 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2386 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: User Management\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services now supports filtering by loginTime. Supported operators are: eq, ne, sw, gt, lt. See Identity Directory API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2387 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Write and proxy write transformation changes\nDescription: A userName mapping that was previously used to ensure that patch operations worked correctly for Local Identity Directory on the Neo environment, is now removed. Currently, you only need to set scim.support.patch.operation = true on the target system.  See Local Identity Directory.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: 26537\n\n--- Record 2388 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Condition and skip update - changed behavior\nDescription: As of September 24, 2024, Identity Provisioning will change the behavior of target transformations that contain a combination of condition and skip operations for updates. For example: Code Syntax  \"condition\": \"$.groups empty false\",\n\"skipOperations\": [\"update\"],   Currently, the skip operation is evaluated before the condition. If any users or groups have been updated in the source system, they are marked as skipped in the logs, and Identity Provisioning does not proceed to evaluate the condition. As a result, users or groups that do not meet the condition are not deleted as they should be.  Following the change, the condition will be evaluated first. Users and groups who do not match the condition will be deleted. After the condition is evaluated, the skip operation will determine whether the remaining users will be skipped or provisioned.  For more information, see Transformation Expressions. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision:", " result, users or groups that do not meet the condition are not deleted as they should be.  Following the change, the condition will be evaluated first. Users and groups who do not match the condition will be deleted. After the condition is evaluated, the skip operation will determine whether the remaining users will be skipped or provisioned.  For more information, see Transformation Expressions. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2389 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: isValidEmail function supports new value\nDescription: The conditional function isValidEmail can now accept the following value $.emails[*].value. In cases where users have multiple emails, this function will validate each email in the emails array.  For more information, see Transformation Functions. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2390 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Read and proxy read transformation changes\nDescription: The mapping which omits the display of groups under the user entity is removed from the default read and proxy read transformations of the Identity Authentication connector. This makes possible filtering users by groups display name when using condition in the target system.  For more information, see Identity Authentication. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-20\nValid as Of: 2024-08-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1111 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: REMINDER: Removal of SAP Java Buildpack 1\nDescription: We want to remind you that SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and is going to be removed from SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025.  Background and Motivation:  SAP Java Buildpack 2 is generally available (GA) since March 2024 and provides support for the latest and greatest versions of Java (17 and 21), Tomcat (10.1), and TomEE (10.0).  SAP Java Buildpack 1, on the other hand, supports older versions of Java (8, 11), Tomcat 9, an SAP-patched version of TomEE 7 (which reached EoL in March 2021), and SapMachine 11 (which also reached EoL in December 2024).  Our goal is to focus our efforts on delivering highly-requested new features, reducing technical debt, and boosting product quality and security.  As a result, SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025.   Action:    If you have applications running on sap_java_buildpack, you need to migrate them to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta as soon as possible.   To learn how, see: Migrate your Applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2  Timeline:  We plan to support SAP Java Buildpack 1 until June 30, 2025, and then it will be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment.  Applications that haven’t been migrated to SAP Java Buildpack 2 by then might continue to run but will fail if being restaged or redeployed.  In H1 of 2025, new releases of SAP Java Buildpack 1 will be only made for critical security updates and bug fixes.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-03\nValid as Of: 2025-04-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1112 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New troubleshooting topic containing information about issues that can arise when transporting Multitarget Applications (MTAs) in Cloud Foundry.\nDescription: See:   Troubleshooting Issues when Transporting Multitarget Applications (MTAs)  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-03\nValid as Of: 2025-04-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1113 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Cloud Transport Management service available on new data centers.\nDescription: SAP Cloud Transport Management service is now also available in the following regions:  Amazon Web Services in the Brazil (São Paulo) region  Google Cloud in the Japan (Osaka) region  Google Cloud in the Australia Southeast (Sydney) region  Google Cloud in the Europe (Frankfurt) region  See:   SAP Cloud Transport Management in SAP Discovery Center  Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-03\nValid as Of: 2025-04-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1114 ---\nComponent: Feature Flags Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Environments\nDescription: You can now enable/disable feature flags, and set different behaviors and delivery strategies for a flag, depending on the environment (landscape) you're deploying your applications on.   For more information, see: Concepts → Environments\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-27\nValid as Of: 2025-04-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Reco