k Zone editions in parallel in a given SAP BTP subaccount. Trying to subscribe to multiple editions, for example both to standard and advanced editions in the same subaccount, will result in an error.   Note   Existing subscriptions are not impacted by this restriction and continue to work as before.  If you're interested in upgrading from the foundation service plan to the standard service plan, you can use the Updatesubscription option in the SAP BTP cockpit.  Note that the Updateoption is only available if the subaccount has entitlements to both the foundation and standard service plans.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413B\n\n--- Record 1570 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP SuccessFactors\nDescription: SAP SuccessFactors has been removed from the list of supported content providers in SAP Help Portal, as it was added accidentally.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-23\nValid as Of: 2025-01-23\nVersion: 2413B\n\n", "--- Record 2181 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Property Required for Using SAP Task Center\nDescription: If you are using SAP Task Center together with SAP Build Process Automation, you must set an additional property in your Identity_Authentication_Connectivity_IDS destination as follows:    If SAP Build Process Automation and SAP Task Center are in the same subaccount, set the wfs.tc.local property to true.      If SAP Build Process Automation and SAP Task Center are in different subaccounts, set the wfs.tc.local property to false.      For more information, see SAP Note 3522594 .  If you don’t set this property, the end users might be able to access their SAP Build Process Automation tasks, but some actions might not be available in the Web app of SAP Task Center.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-02\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2182 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional Property Required for SAP Build Process Automation\nDescription: If you are using SAP Build Process Automation as task provider, you must set up an additional property in your SAP Build Process Automation  Identity_Authentication_Connectivity_IDS destination, as follows:       If SAP Build Process Automation and SAP Task Center are in the same subaccount, set the wfs.tc.local property to true.      If SAP Build Process Automation and SAP Task Center are in different subaccounts, set the wfs.tc.local property to false.      For more information, see SAP Note 3522594 .  If you don’t set this property, the end users might be able to access their SAP Build Process Automation tasks, but some actions might not be available in the Web app.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-02\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2183 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: 26738\n\n--- Record 2184 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Bugfix regarding ABAP Application Names\nDescription: An issue was resolved that caused failures of SAP Fiori for the ABAP Platform jobs due to application names with blank values. Now, only application names that adhere to the specification can be added.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-02\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2185 ---\nComponent: Inbound Nota Fiscal\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support to Simplified CT-e\nDescription: CT-e Basic Process and CT-e Flex Process have been changed to support Simplified CT-e, according to SEFAZ Technical Note 2024.002 1.01 Version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-03\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2186 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Return Condition Rate in Document Currency for Group Conditions\nDescription: To return the condition rate converted into the document currency the structure conditionRateConverted was added to conditions response of stateless pricing and rateConverted was added to the conditions response of document pricing. A null value used to be returned for group conditions with group key routines. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-01\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2187 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Task Center Improvements\nDescription: Notifications are now displayed consistently for all supported task providers without being deleted every 24 hours.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-02\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2188 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Substitution Management for Business Administrators Enabled in the Task Center Administration App\nDescription: In the Task Center Administration app business administrators can create substitution rules on behalf of end users, and manage existing substitution rules, created by end users.  For more information, see Using Substitution Management for Business Administrators.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-02\nValid as Of: 2024-10-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2189 ---\nComponent: Personalized Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code and performance improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-01\nValid as Of: 2024-10-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2190"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_f823f276039bbdbd1ca910bb3b860c5fe880e106550b0f733113f67142b3db90_v2"}